Yes, it is possible to block an issue from moving to another column if all items in a checklist are done marked as done in a Jira board workflow. You can use the "Checklist" field and set up a custom validation rule to achieve this.

Here's how you can do it:

1. Create a custom field of type "Checklist" in your Jira project. Let's call it "Task List".
2. Add all the tasks related to that issue in the "Task List" field.
3. Go to the "Workflows" tab of your Jira project and click on the workflow you want to edit.
4. Click on the "Transitions" tab and select the transition that moves the issue to the next column.
5. In the "Validation" section, click on the "Add Validation" button and choose "Custom".
6. Give your validation a name and select the "Checklist" field as the source field.
7. In the "Validation Expression" field, enter the following expression:
```
function() {
  var taskList = issue.customfield_10000; // Replace 10000 with the ID of your "Task List" field
  return taskList.every(function(task) {
    return task.status === "done";
  });
}
```
This expression will check if all tasks in the "Task List" field are marked as "done". If they are, the issue will not be allowed to move to the next column.

8. Save your workflow and test it to make sure it works as expected.

Note: The ID of your "Task List" field might be different depending on your project setup. You can find the ID by going to the "Fields" tab of your Jira project and looking for the "ID" column.

