Certainly! Here's a simple JavaScript function that switches the order of adjectives in a sentence:

```javascript
function swapAdjectives(sentence) {
  const words = sentence.split(" ");
  const adjectives = words.filter(word => word === "beautiful" || word === "green");
  const reversedAdjectives = adjectives.reverse();
  const updatedSentence = words.map((word, index) => {
    if (adjectives.includes(word)) {
      return reversedAdjectives[index];
    } else {
      return word;
    }
  }).join(" ");
  return updatedSentence;
}

const inputSentence = "Beautiful green trees are in the park";
const outputSentence = swapAdjectives(inputSentence);
console.log(outputSentence); // Output: "Green beautiful trees are in the park"
```

This function takes a sentence as input and splits it into an array of words. It then filters out the adjectives ("beautiful" and "green") and reverses their order. Finally, it iterates through the words array and replaces each adjective with its corresponding reversed adjective. The updated sentence is then joined back into a string and returned.

