edge_image_y = conv2(double(gaussian_filtered_image), sobel_y, 'same');

% Combine edges in both directions
edge_image = sqrt(edge_image_x.^2 + edge_image_y.^2);

% Display edge image
imshow(edge_image);
```

This code first applies a Gaussian filter with a kernel size of 3x3 and a standard deviation of 0.5 to the input image. Then, it applies the Sobel operator in both x and y directions to the filtered image to extract the edges. Finally, it combines the edges in both directions and displays the result.

