To identify the tense used in a given sentence, we can use regular expressions and a lookup table of tense patterns. Here's a MATLAB code that can accomplish this task:

```matlab
% Define the regular expression patterns for each tense
tense_patterns = {
    'present': {'Present Simple', 'Present Continuous', 'Present Perfect'},
    'past': {'Past Simple', 'Past Continuous', 'Past Perfect'},
    'future': {'Future Simple', 'Future Continuous', 'Future Perfect'},
    'conditional': {'Conditional I', 'Conditional II'},
    'perfect': {'Perfect Simple', 'Perfect Continuous', 'Perfect Perfect'},
    'passive': {'Passive Simple', 'Passive Continuous', 'Passive Perfect'}
};

% Define the function to identify the tense
function tense = identify_tense(sentence)
    % Split the sentence into words
    words = strsplit(sentence, ' ');

    % Iterate through the tense patterns and check if any match
    for pattern, tenses in tense_patterns
        for tense_name in tenses
            if regexp(words, pattern, 'match')
                tense = tense_name;
                break;
            end
        end
    end
end

% Test the function with the given sentence
