To set up Auth0 SSO (Single Sign-On) for multiple React apps, follow these steps:

1. Sign up for an Auth0 account and create a new application.
2. In the Auth0 dashboard, navigate to the "Applications" tab and select your newly created application.
3. Click on the "Settings" tab and scroll down to the "Redirect URI" section. Add the following redirect URI format for each of your React apps: `http://localhost:3000/callback`
4. In your React apps, install the `@auth0/auth0-react` package using npm or yarn.
5. Create a new file called `auth0-config.js` in your React app's root directory and add the following configuration:
```javascript
import auth0 from '@auth0/auth0-react';

const auth0ClientId = 'your_client_id';
const auth0Domain = 'your_domain.com';

auth0.configure({
  domain: auth0Domain,
  clientId: auth0ClientId,
  responseType: 'token id_token',
  scope: 'openid profile email',
  redirectUri: 'http://localhost:3000/callback',
});
```
Replace `your_client_id` with the client ID you obtained from the Auth0 dashboard and `your_domain.com` with your Auth0 domain.
6. In your React app's main component, import the `auth0-config.js` file and use the `Auth0Provider` component to wrap your app:
```javascript
import { Auth0Provider } from '@auth0/auth0-react';
import auth0Config from './auth0-config';

function App() {
  return (
    <Auth0Provider {...auth0Config}>
      {/* Your app content goes here */}
    </Auth0Provider>
  );
}

export default App;
```
7. Now, when users access your React apps, they will be prompted to log in with their Auth0 credentials. Once logged in, they will be able to access all your React apps without having to re-enter their credentials.

Note: Make sure to handle the authentication flow appropriately in your React apps, such as redirecting

Here's a C function that converts an array of arguments (argv) to a null-terminated string:

```c
#include <stdio.h>
#include <stdlib.h>

char *argv_to_cstring(int argc, char *argv[]) {
    int i;
    size_t len = 0;
    char *str = malloc(argc * sizeof(char));

    if (!str) {
        return NULL;
    }

    for (i = 0; i < argc; i++) {
        len += strlen(argv[i]) + 1; // Add space for the null terminator
    }

    str[0] = '\0';
    for (i = 0; i < argc; i++) {
        strcat(str, argv[i]);
        strcat(str, " ");
    }

    str[len - 1] = '\0'; // Remove the last space character

    return str;
}

int main(int argc, char *argv[]) {
    char *cstring = argv_to_cstring(argc, argv);
    if (cstring) {
        printf("Converted argument string: %s\n", cstring);
        free(cstring);
    } else {
        printf("Error allocating memory.\n");
    }

    return 0;
}
```

